sbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUZAWA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AIMOTO, KOHJIROH</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN ENERGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUZAWA, KENJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AIMOTO KOHJIROH</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUZAWA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AIMOTO, KOHJIROH</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUZAWA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of isomerizing a feed material which has not undergone any special pretreatment such as desulfurization or a method of isomerizing a hydrocarbon using hydrogen containing a sulfur compound. The isomerization method is characterized by contacting hydrogen and a raw hydrocarbon containing sulfur compounds in an amount of 10 to 500 ppm in terms of sulfur amount by weight with a solid acid catalyst comprising a support containing a part consisting of zirconia and/or hydrated zirconia and a sulfuric acid ingredient deposited on the support. The isomerized hydrocarbon thus obtained preferably has a content of organic sulfur compounds of 10 ppm or lower in terms of sulfur amount by weight.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé d'isomérisation d'une charge d'alimentation n'ayant subi aucun prétraitement spécial, tel qu'une désulfuration, ou un procédé d'isomérisation d'un hydrocarbure au moyen d'hydrogène contenant un composé soufre. Ce procédé d'isomérisation est caractérisé par l'étape suivante consistant à mettre en contact de l'hydrogène et un hydrocarbure brut contenant des composés soufre dont la quantité pondérale de soufre est comprise entre 10 et 550 ppm, avec un catalyseur acide solide comprenant un support, dont une partie se compose de zircone et/ou de zircone hydratée, et un ingrédient à base d'acide sulfurique déposé sur le support. L'hydrocarbure isomérisé ainsi obtenu possède, de préférence, une teneur en composés organiques soufre de 10 ppm ou moins en terme de quantité pondérale de soufre.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>